Karabas Go C64
==============

This repository is a port of the Commodore 64 to the Karabas Go / Mini /
Mini G boards.

Main license: GNU General Public License v3.0 (see LICENSE), unless a file
carries a different notice.

The SID 8580 implementation in src/rtl/sid_mister8580/ is derived from the
MiSTer SID / reDIP-SID work and is covered by the CERN Open Hardware Licence
Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal (see LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-2.0.txt).

Third-party components and their authors:

- FPGA64 by Peter Wendrich and contributors (GPL-3.0):
  src/rtl/c64/cpu_6510.vhd, fpga64_buslogic.vhd, fpga64_keyboard.vhd,
  fpga64_rgbcolor.vhd, fpga64_sid_iec.vhd, video_vicII_656x.vhd,
  video_sync.vhd and related files.
- MiSTer C64 by Sorgelig and contributors (GPL-3.0): the C64 machine,
  cartridge, SID and VIC integration.
- 1541 implementation by Dar (darfpga) and contributors.
- Shared Karabas FPGA modules:
  https://github.com/andykarpov/karabas-go-modules (git submodule).
- Karabas firmware/tools: https://github.com/andykarpov/karabas-go-firmware.

ROM data: the Commodore 64 KERNAL, BASIC and character generator and the
1541 ROM are property of their respective owners. They are build inputs for
the local core and are not relicensed by this repository.
